Week 2 is important for VLSI and EDA because Physical Design and STA depend on understanding the structure of RTL.

FSMs, counters, FIFO pointers, and registers create sequential boundaries.

Combinational logic between registers becomes timing paths.

This means the distinction between combinational logic and sequential logic is not only a coding issue. It affects synthesis, timing analysis, setup checks, hold checks, and timing closure.

Understanding these RTL structures now will make it easier to study RTL-to-GDS flow, STA, and OpenROAD later.

